+# Cloud IAM / KMS Integration for COSIGN keys
+
+Purpose
+- Document recommended integration points to store and use COSIGN KMS keys securely and enforce key usage via cloud IAM.
+
+Recommendations
+- Use your cloud KMS (AWS KMS, GCP KMS, Azure Key Vault) to host signing keys and grant least-privilege access to runner/service accounts.
+- Use short-lived credentials for CI runs (OIDC), and bind KMS key usage to specific principals (Platform Owner / CI role).
+- Example: set COSIGN_KMS_URI=kms://projects/<proj>/locations/global/keyRings/<ring>/cryptoKeys/<key>
+- In GitHub Actions, prefer OIDC and not long lived secrets; use action identity to request temporary access to KMS when signing artifacts.
+- Log all cosign sign operations and record signed artifact metadata into Rekor; record manifest with ops.sdk.evidence_sdk for audit.
+
+Operational checklist
+- Ensure KMS key rotation policy is defined.
+- Audit who has Encrypt/Sign/Decrypt permissions in KMS.
+- Enable KMS activity logs and ship to central logging (Cloud Logging / Splunk / ELK).
