+# Top operational risks & mitigations
+
+Risk: Unvalidated timing on real topology
+- Likelihood: High until RT sweeps are run on representative hardware
+- Mitigation:
+  - Run ops/validation/run_hw_validation_pipeline.py across all ECU/bridge topologies
+  - Record signed rt_slo_proof bundles and keep them in S3
+  - Add p99 & safe_stop metrics to Prometheus/Grafana
+
+Risk: Blocking certification due to unresolved formal counterexamples or waveform mismatches
+- Mitigation:
+  - Run ops/robotics/control/hil_formal_closure_runner.py to drive HIL + Apalache closures
+  - Triage counterexamples as owner-assigned tasks; add failing scenarios to backlog and re-run
+  - Keep signed HIL bundles with waveform compare outputs for certifier
+
+Risk: Perception long-tail compute/time burden
+- Mitigation:
+  - Use scale_orchestrator.py and Argo to parallelize simulation packs
+  - Prioritize scenario families and incremental retraining
+  - Use spot/preemptible compute for large sim runs and keep evidence artifacts small (NDJSON references)
+
+Risk: CI gates ineffective if builders not hardened
+- Mitigation:
+  - Use builder_rollout_manager.sh and ops/ci/builders/auto_harden_builders.sh to onboard builders
+  - Enforce ops/ci/promotion_gate/enforce_builder_provenance.py in staging & production workflows
+
+Risk: Carbon enforcement false positives
+- Mitigation:
+  - Run production_monitor_and_tune.sh for observation window and set thresholds conservatively
+  - Document override workflow and require cosign-signed artifact from Platform Owner
+
+General ops/security mitigations
+- Integrate KMS & OIDC for signing; centralize logs; run vulnerability scans and third-party penetration tests; rotate keys.
+
